# ARK Staff App Reset

Full doc: `ark-mobile/docs/staff-app-reset.md`

## Product rule

Do not build features because the backend has data. Build only the workflow the staff member is trying to complete.

Every screen answers: Where am I? · Current condition? · What next? · Why? · What happened? · What can I do?

## Role homes (not one nav for everyone)

| Profile | Primary question | Home centers on |
|---------|------------------|-----------------|
| **Technician** | What do I inspect or repair next? | Assigned ROs → RO workspace → inspection points |
| **Advisor** | Who needs a response or decision? | Conversations, check-in, approvals, calls |
| **Manager** | What needs attention across the shop? | Attention board, blockers, ready pickup |

## Technician — do not expose

Global Conversations tab · shop Attention · estimates · payments · dashboards · check-in (unless explicitly earned)

Comms only **inside assigned RO workspace**.

## Advisor — do not expose

Technician inspection entry flow · raw checklist unless reviewing · production-only controls

## RO workspace

Center of technician work. Enter once, stay until done. Inspection points (condition, photos, measurements, notes) — not freeform findings as primary.

Deep links (Attention, check-in, My Work) → `RepairOrderWorkspaceScreen`, not legacy RO detail.

## Shell contract

`home_profile` + `capabilities` from `MobileUserPresenter` — Flutter gates tabs from server, no `if (technician)` nav in Dart.

## Do not build (Phase 1)

Settings · profile pages · analytics dashboards · push/Firebase · AI summaries · desktop estimate builder · payment UI · customer portal — unless floor evidence earns them.

## Acceptance

Technician completes inspection on assigned RO without desktop. Advisor responds and sends next link without desktop. Manager sees who needs attention without searching.

Wrong: same workflow for every role · module list feeling. Right: each role answers their next operational question.

